  "notes": "{貶|おとし}める is a transitive ichidan verb. It carries a strongly negative connotation and implies deliberate belittling or degradation.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{貶|おとし}めている describes an ongoing act of disparagement.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- AをBと{貶|おとし}める (disparage A as B)\n- Aを{貶|おとし}める (put down A)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人|ひと}を{貶|おとし}める (disparage someone)\n- {名誉|めいよ}を{貶|おとし}める (damage someone's honor)\n- {価値|かち}を{貶|おとし}める (diminish the value of)\n\nMore literary and formal than {馬鹿|ばか}にする or {見下|みくだ}す. Often used in written contexts discussing discrimination, bullying, or ethical behavior.",
